spu-neon-fixups.patch: on top of pending/perf-spu-runtime.patch (2026-10-23).

NEON csflt/cuflt/fi (PS3_SPU_NEON_CVT) and a vector form of the fa/fm/fma
fix-ups (PS3_SPU_NEON_FIX: every lane exact in double -- exponent-0 words,
extended range, exponent gaps over 29, out-of-range results, fma sums rounded
onto a 24-bit boundary), both live toggles, both bit-exact against the scalar
lanes (tests/test_spu_fi_neon.c, test_spu_cflt_fast.c, test_spu_float_neon.c:
24M adversarial lanes through the fix-ups). SPU_FLOATFIX_STATS on the walk:
fa gap 1.68G lanes a run, fma zero-a/zero-b/ext 1.5G, fm 0.3G. Live A/B
(headless walk): NEON_FIX +0.2% fps (10 pairs), NEON_CVT +0.2% (3 pairs):
inside the noise, so it is left out of the toolkit patch, as
spu-neon-helpers.patch was.

